[Music]  as omicron concerns continue thousands  of unlv students headed back to class  today unlike during the fall semester a  vaccine mandate is not in place joe  moeller spoke to students today he joins  us live on campus with what they had to  share joe  occasionally it was a pretty busy day  here on the unlv campus just behind us  here some students are actually leaving  for the day we talked to a handful of  them most of them feel pretty safe with  the precautions in place but some would  like to see that mandate back in place  students are back on campus for spring  semester 2022 about 40 percent of  classes remain virtual during the fall  semester a vaccine mandate for students  was in place that came to an end after  the legislative commission said it was  not permanent with a recent spike in  cases students still feel comfortable as  more than 90 percent of them are all  vaccinated me and my family got the  vaccine so i'm  good on all that if no people don't want  to get then it's fine it's up to them  one of my professors already threatened  us that if we don't wear a mask during  an exam or like we don't wear it in his  class he will kick us at like by the  second time he warns us friday the board  of regents sent a letter to lawmakers  pushing for a mandate to be put in place  back out here live it is up to the board  of health to make the mandate i checked  into that there is currently no public  hearing scheduled on that topic as of  now but there is still that vaccine  mandate in place for staff here on  campus reporting live at unlv joe mohler  live local now thank you

